   200	Two clean re-readings, both new here and both machine-checked.
   201	
   202	> **LEMMA L2 (genus of the net).** Let `g_net` be the geometric genus of a general
   203	> member of the net (= of the projective closure of a generic fibre of a generic
   204	> `lambda P + mu Q`). Then, for **every** dominant `F`,
   205	> ```text
   206	>            Z . K_X  =  2 g_net  -  N  -  2 .
