   208	> *Proof.* By Bertini the general member is smooth off the base points, so its
   209	> only singularities are the (infinitely near) `p_i`, with multiplicities `a_i`;
   210	> hence `p_a(D) - g_net = sum_i a_i(a_i-1)/2`. Substitute `(D1)` and
   211	> `Z.K_X = sum a_i - 3D`. ∎
   212	>
   213	> **COROLLARY.** Under Keller + `H2`, `g_net = (2 - N - kappa + n(W-S))/2 >= 0`,
   214	> so `n(W-S) >= N + kappa - 2` and `n(W-S) = N + kappa mod 2`.
   215	> `OPEN[ANTICANON-DEFECT]` is **exactly** "is the genus of the generic member of
   216	> the pencil bounded in `N`?" — the question the parallel flagship
   217	> `KELLER-PENCIL-GENUS` owns. This lane hands it over as an identity, and claims
   218	> nothing further about it.
