   183	
   184	Reading of C9: the P-place value data fails the one-place PREcondition
   185	(y has a zero, not a pole, at the place). On a one-place curve every
   186	nonconstant polynomial has its unique pole at the place; y|_C is
   187	nonconstant; so a curve owning a P-place as its ONLY place at infinity
   188	would force y|_C = 0 — absurd. That one-line argument is the content
   189	of C9a; C9b is its semigroup quantification: the only positive reading
   190	of the exponent ladder sits strictly on the LOCAL side of the AM
   191	dichotomy at every step, i.e. the P-places are finite-center-type
   192	branches (y -> 0 along the place, toward the point [1:0:0]).
   193	
   194	## 3. Adjudication
   195	
   196	### 3.1 Fiber tier: outcomes (a) and (b) are structurally unreachable
   197	
   198	The one-place hypothesis attaches to no pinned template object. The
   199	fiber C is irreducible (f primitive, SHEET6-CLASSICAL.md:29-30) with
   200	>= 2 places forced by the template itself (P_1 != P_2, engine C10:
   201	their series split at the characteristic level 32 since
   202	a_1 - a_2 = 2 sqrt3 != 0), >= 4 places on the banked count
   203	(SHEET6-CLASSICAL.md:156), generically 2 + r_B + 42
   204	(GROK-MONODROMY.md:149-174). So (AM-SG) simply does not constrain C,
   205	and no violation of it can kill residue-A — outcome (a) is unreachable.
   206	Equally, no "CONSISTENT with margins" report (b) is honest: the
   207	inequality is not satisfied-with-slack, it is inapplicable, and its
   208	reflected form is violated. The violation is REQUIRED structure: by
   209	(AM-JAC) a Keller counterexample's f must not be one-place, and this
   210	template complies at the strongest (semigroup-certified) level.
   211	
   212	Deformation stability: the reflected-ladder margins are the exponent
   213	gaps m_{i+1} - m_i, which are POSITIVE for every admissible genome
   214	(edges have positive length; any Q-preserving deformation keeps
   215	ascending characteristic levels, i.e. y bounded along every y-side
   216	place — the root-chart convention itself, SHEET6-TEMPLATE.md:63-64).
   217	Hence EVERY genome in this frame stays on the local side: the one-place
   218	instrument cannot come alive at fiber tier for residue-A or for any of
   219	its siblings (the @w4/@w3/@w2 book, SHEET6-DIRECTIONB.md:351-352) under
   220	any deformation of the pinned data. This is a permanent wrong-object

