./xmodel/ideation-20260824T0156Z-grok.md:51:Proof-side, JC2 is still “finite étale endomorphism of \(\mathbb{A}^2\) is an automorphism.” Over \(\mathbb{C}\), constant Jacobian already gives étaleness; finiteness is the missing global assertion. Every honest global rewrite — integrality of \(x,y\) over \(\mathbb{C}[P,Q]\), vanishing of the collision ideal, emptiness of \(A(F)\), regularity of the first \(d\) power traces — is map-by-map equivalent to that missing finiteness. The tried core (GGV farm, Sigray books, D-series) is a necessary-condition mill: it can kill special presentations, not currently close the conjecture. Hybrid GGV→Sigray still owes `G2-PSC`. A pure Sigray route may refuse GGV, and then still owes an independent source, complete landing/coverage, and a bounded/cofinal type menu; type-relative KJN is not that menu. Internal characteristic-zero emptiness for reopened cCa/R1 uses remains absent. External exact terminals on the two Proposition-4.3 residual systems do not prove the GGV reduction/transcription bridge, and do not prove JC2.
