./xmodel/significant-news-ideation-rank4-cycle-grok46-20260830.md:324:**Required hypotheses.** Promoted etale-torsor gate `f5dbad98...`; factoriality of `C[x,y]`; connectedness of the branch; the one-place hypothesis so that a Nagata chart analogous to `div(u)=2P0+P1` exists. The constant-unit lemma is **not** required: a torsion-free `Cl` kills units cubed and Picard 3-torsion together, as in the nodal control.
./xmodel/significant-news-ideation-rank4-cycle-grok46-20260830.md:326:**First falsification test.** Take the next one-place curve after the nodal cubic: an immersive polynomial parametrization with one ordinary node and one `A2` (affine `delta=2`, infinity type `T(2,5)`). This curve cannot be an `S4` branch, so it is a method control, not a possible horn member: `det=5` makes the boundary map to `Hom(H1(Sigma_2),C3)` zero, and a surviving anti-invariant 3-torsion class would be purely affine. Compute `Cl` of its double plane by the same Nagata localization. A 3-torsion class that extends over the singularities is a counter-control and stops a blanket vanishing theorem. If `Cl` remains torsion-free, move the live computation to a `delta=3` embedding (the actual remaining cell), not to a larger random family.
